# Files inside the assets directory that must NOT be uploaded to Workers.
# Same syntax as .gitignore. Astro copies this file verbatim from public/ to the
# root of dist/, which is where Wrangler looks for it.
#
# It excludes nothing today, and that is the correct state: dist/ is built fresh
# from sources and contains no node_modules, no .git and no source maps. The file
# exists for the opposite reason — to say what must never be added to it.
#
#   NEVER add _headers or _redirects.
#
# Cloudflare's own migration guide lists them as candidates, and following that
# advice here would be silent and expensive. On Workers those two files are not
# served as assets at all: they are parsed, and their rules are applied to asset
# responses. Excluding them from the upload does not stop them being public — they
# already are not — it stops them existing. The site would lose its Content
# Security Policy, its cache policy and its playground rewrite, and every page
# would keep answering 200.
#
# Also deliberately absent: *.br and *.gz.
#
# The Blazor publish emits a pre-compressed twin of every framework file — 96 of
# the artefact's 153 files, 6.3 MiB — and the .NET loader never requests one, as
# a search of the published loader confirms. They are dead weight on a host that
# compresses at the edge, and excluding them would cut the upload by roughly two
# thirds.
#
# The question that kept them was whether the host compresses application/wasm on
# the way out. Against the local runtime it does, measured rather than assumed:
# 3,002,102 bytes become 1,197,764 with Content-Encoding: br. The twins are
# therefore unused *and* unnecessary — and they are publicly fetchable at their own
# URLs into the bargain.
#
# They stay for one remaining reason, and it is small: the local runtime is not the
# edge. Excluding them on the strength of a local measurement risks shipping a
# 2.9 MiB runtime uncompressed against a 3 MiB budget for the whole first load, and
# the artefact's own checks would not notice, because they measure files rather than
# transfers.
#
# That is now one command away from settled, against the deployed site:
#
#     scripts/check-served-headers.sh https://justdummies.io
#
# If it reports the payload compressed there too, delete this paragraph and add
# *.br and *.gz below.
